  "sourceInterpretation": "The original official image reports ESP-IDFv6.1-dirty; its exact private revision is unknown. Fixed public IDF6.1 fff9895c82d744c7237be8847347bdd1b07c6643 headers/HAL establish registers,clock ratio and software sequence. Retained September2026 TRM lists System Timer as to-be-added,27percent. Functional synchronization and simultaneous-edge ordering are not silicon-validated.",
  "semantics": {
    "clock": "SYSTIMER_CTRL0 20587120: independent APB and source gates,reset,XTAL/RC_FAST mux. Counter source divided by exactly2.5. CONF.CLK_EN controls automatic register-clock policy,not counter ticking.",
    "counter": "Two52-bit units; masked high loads,WT apply,first-edge snapshot,valid only after real clock input. Reads and writes to SS/WTC status never invent work. Software stall latches feed configured stall inputs; WFI is separate.",
    "alarm": "Three active/shadow comparators,one-shot missed-target compensation,periodic modular target progression. RAW independent of ENA,cleared only by paired CLR. Every actual event is routed as documented source33/34/35 through each hart matrix/CLIC.",
    "time": "Explicit systimer-from-cpu option converts one nominal CPU quantum per dual-hart round,with fractional phase across frequency changes. Optional direct timer-domain tick input. A fully waiting machine remains Waiting; no automatic idle scheduler.",
    "permissions": "HP_PERI1_PMS offset60 controls actual timer accesses; clock-control permissions remain in HP_SYS_CLKRST domain.",
    "unsupported": [
      "FORCE_NORST/global reset precedence",
      "Zero-period comparator",
      "ETM consumers and sleep transitions",
      "Cycle-accurate synchronization/oscillator rates",
      "Automatic idle-time advancement",
      "Complete Plus board/display"
    ]
  },
